@startuml fig_3_purchase_workflow
!theme plain
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI", "Arial", sans-serif
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 6

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #2B2D42
    ActorBorderColor #2B2D42
    LifeLineBorderColor #4A5568
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #EDF2F7
    ParticipantBorderColor #2B2D42
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    BoxBorderColor #2B2D42
    BoxBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
}

title Figure 3: Customer Purchase & Digital Delivery Workflow (In-Process Execution)

actor "Customer" as User
participant "Frontend Node\n(Next.js Client)" as Frontend

box "Backend Node: Modular Monolith Runtime" #F4F6F8
    participant "Catalog\nModule" as Mod_Catalog
    participant "Commerce\nModule" as Mod_Commerce
    participant "Payment\nHandler" as Payment_Sub
    participant "Prisma ORM\nData Layer" as Data_Layer
    participant "Storage\nService" as Storage_Sub
end box

participant "Midtrans\nGateway" as Midtrans
database "PostgreSQL\nDatabase" as Postgres
database "MinIO\nObject Store" as Minio

User -> Frontend : 1. Selects 3D Model & Clicks "Purchase"
Frontend -> Mod_Commerce : 2. POST /api/commerce/checkout {model_id, license_tier}

note over Mod_Catalog, Mod_Commerce #E2E8F0
  In-Process Function Call (Zero Network Latency):
  Commerce module invokes Catalog directly in memory
  to verify asset state, ownership, and pricing.
end note

Mod_Commerce -> Mod_Catalog : 3. validate_asset_and_pricing(model_id, license_tier)
Mod_Catalog --> Mod_Commerce : 4. Return {is_active: true, price: 150000, artist_id: ...}

Mod_Commerce -> Payment_Sub : 5. create_payment_intent(order_details)
Payment_Sub -> Midtrans : 6. HTTPS POST /snap/v1/transactions (Create Snap Token)
Midtrans --> Payment_Sub : 7. Return {snap_token, redirect_url}
Payment_Sub --> Mod_Commerce : 8. In-process return snap token
Mod_Commerce --> Frontend : 9. Response {snap_token}

User -> Frontend : 10. Completes Payment in Snap Popup
Midtrans -> Payment_Sub : 11. HTTPS POST /api/webhooks/midtrans (payment_success)

group Unified Database Transaction (ACID Boundary)
    Payment_Sub -> Mod_Commerce : 12. handle_payment_settlement(order_id)
    Mod_Commerce -> Data_Layer : 13. execute_transaction()
    Data_Layer -> Postgres : 14. BEGIN TRANSACTION;\nUPDATE "Order" SET status = 'PAID';\nINSERT INTO "Purchase" (user_id, model_id, license);\nUPDATE "User" SET balance = balance + net_share WHERE id = artist_id;\nCOMMIT;
    Postgres --> Data_Layer : 15. Transaction Confirmed
    Data_Layer --> Mod_Commerce : 16. Settlement Confirmed
end

Mod_Commerce -> Storage_Sub : 17. generate_presigned_download_url(model_id, user_id)
Storage_Sub -> Minio : 18. S3 Sign: GetObject (model_key, expires_in=3600)
Minio --> Storage_Sub : 19. Signed URL string
Storage_Sub --> Mod_Commerce : 20. Return Signed URL

Mod_Commerce --> Frontend : 21. Event / Status: Purchase Confirmed + Signed URL
Frontend --> User : 22. Display "Download Unlocked" & Direct File Link

@enduml
